# Python bytecode from running scripts/merge_tools.py
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool run logs. merge_tools.py writes a new timestamped log on every lint/drugs/paed
# run, so these accumulate without bound and dirty the working tree on every branch —
# which is how 11 of them and a .pyc were swept into commits by `git add -A`.
# The durable record of a run is _meta/OVERNIGHT_REPORT.md and _meta/RUN_STATE.md,
# not these files.
# Anchored at the repo root by git, because the pattern contains a slash — which is
# exactly why 14 logs survived inside Corpus A/_meta/runs/ on 2026-08-31. The tool now
# resolves the vault root itself (scripts/merge_tools.py vault_root), so logs cannot be
# written into a corpus at all; this second pattern is the belt to that braces.
_meta/runs/
**/_meta/runs/
